WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.466
<v DANA>Here's a quick one about sharps
containers. Say you walk up to one, and

00:00:04.466 --> 00:00:09.633
<v DANA>it's past the fill line. The used blades
are crowded right at the opening. What do

00:00:09.633 --> 00:00:10.080
<v DANA>you do?

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:15.200
<v RAY>Well, it's tempting to press them down to
make room, or to squeeze one more in.

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:17.120
<v DANA>[skeptical] What's wrong with pressing
them down?

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:21.330
<v RAY>[matter-of-fact] Pressing down puts your
hand right NEXT to used blades. When a

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:25.290
<v RAY>container reaches its fill line, it's
full, so you use another designated

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:25.840
<v RAY>container.

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:28.960
<v DANA>Okay. Anything else I should be looking
for?

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:33.897
<v RAY>Yes, a sharp that's out of place. That
could be on a work surface, hidden in

00:00:33.897 --> 00:00:39.031
<v RAY>other material, or in the regular trash.
Either way, it puts the next person at

00:00:39.031 --> 00:00:39.360
<v RAY>risk.

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:42.320
<v DANA>So there are really two different things
to spot.

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:47.200
<v RAY>You know, that's exactly it, and spotting
either one early prevents injuries.

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:48.400
<v DANA>Good to know.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:52.480
<v RAY>[warmly] Just remember that when a
container is at the fill line, it's FULL.

